
for the whole system wokring off four componenets it starts wiht the systems state including all of the modules: 

S(t) = [H(t), O(t), C(t), D(t)]

H health 
O optimization 
C configuration 
D defence 

t is the vector for time. 

evolution of system 

S(t+1) = S(t) + A(t) + N(t)

A(t) being autonomic action whihc would be the actions of the four modules 
N(t) is the noise/ disturbance like whats trigggering the action of the modules to start like traffic spikes, hardware failures etc 


self-healing 

H(t) = 1 - (W(e)E(t) + w(l)L(t) + w(f)F(t))

E(t) is error rate 
L(t) is latency 
F(t) is failure probability 
wieght sum to <(and equal) to  1 

if error rise the health drops and if a failure spikes the health drops which triggers 

if H(t) < tau -> repair action 

tau is the safety threshold

and example of this would be 

if health < 0.7; 
     restart_service()

after the repair you have 

H(t+1) = H(t) + alpha(1 - H(t))

 i cannot type the alpah symbol for preferential connection parameter nor copy it in. 
 a smaller alpha is a slower recovery and a larger alpja is a aggressive repair. 
