autonomic resilience simulation framework 

at the core the closed system loop will act as 

environment - metrics - decision engine - action - new state 

the system state model with master vector as made: 

S(t) = [H(t), O(t), C(t), D(t)]

eg
state = {
    latency 
    error_rate 
    cpu_usage 
    memory_usage 
    config_valid
    anomaly_score 
  }

failure injection for example node crashes, traffic spikes, memory leaks and malicious requests

N(t) ~ P(λ) 
disturbance is sampled from a probability disribution 


to compute health of the system - 

H(t) = 1 - (0.4E(t) + 0.3L(t) + 0.3F(t))

cost funcion 

J(t) = alphaC(t) + betaL(t) + cE(t)

anomaly scoring 

Z = x - μ/ σ
if the threshold is les than Z then system is susipcious. 

decision engine draft basic 

IF anomaly high -> defend 
ELSE IF health low -> heal 
ELSE IF cost high -> optimise 
ELSE -> maintain 

which would write as A(t) = π(S(t))

for t in time_steps: 
    inject_disturbance()
    measure_metric()
    compute_health()
    compute_anomaly()
    detect_anomaly()
    action = policy(state)
    apply(action) 
    log_results()
    

      
 
